61
00:01:58,030 --> 00:01:59,260
Hold one dollar, and you

62
00:01:59,380 --> 00:02:00,470
gain one dollar per year.

63
00:02:00,820 --> 00:02:02,320
Hold two, and you gain two.

64
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:04,347
Draw it as a graph,

65
00:02:04,373 --> 00:02:05,670
and you get e to the t.

66
00:02:05,930 --> 00:02:07,520
At every point, the slope of

67
00:02:07,600 --> 00:02:08,780
the curve equals its height.

68
00:02:09,730 --> 00:02:11,090
Or picture it as motion.

69
00:02:11,370 --> 00:02:13,300
A point on a line, whose velocity

70
00:02:13,420 --> 00:02:15,020
is always equal to its position.

71
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,630
The farther it gets, the faster it runs.

72
00:02:18,490 --> 00:02:19,690
Hold on to that sentence.

73
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:21,670
Velocity equals position.

74
00:02:22,040 --> 00:02:23,180
It is the heart of e.

75
00:02:23,450 --> 00:02:24,680
And we are about to change

76
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:25,720
just one word of it.

77
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,600
Now for i.

78
00:02:28,920 --> 00:02:30,340
Forget the idea that i is

79
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:31,760
a number that cannot exist.

80
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,370
Instead, think of numbers as actions.

81
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:36,850
Lay every number out on a line.

82
00:02:37,170 --> 00:02:39,000
Multiplying by two is an action.

83
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:40,840
It stretches the line, pushing

84
00:02:40,920 --> 00:02:42,600
everything twice as far from zero.

85
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:44,790
Multiplying by one half squeezes it.

86
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:47,520
And multiplying by negative one?

87
00:02:47,780 --> 00:02:49,370
Three goes to negative three.

88
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:51,280
Negative two goes to two.

89
00:02:51,510 --> 00:02:53,100
Every number swings to

90
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:54,440
the other side of zero.

91
00:02:54,710 --> 00:02:55,880
It is a half turn.

92
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:57,960
Remember that.

93
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,570
Negative one is a half turn.

94
00:02:59,930 --> 00:03:00,950
It is going to matter.

95
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:04,030
Now here is the question that i answers.

96
00:03:04,530 --> 00:03:06,460
What action, done twice,

97
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,370
gives a half turn?

98
00:03:08,330 --> 00:03:09,320
Not a stretch.

99
00:03:09,650 --> 00:03:11,350
Two stretches only stretch further.

100
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:13,160
But a quarter turn, done

101
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:14,710
twice, is a half turn.

102
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:18,020
So let the line become a plane, where

103
00:03:18,060 --> 00:03:19,740
numbers can point in any direction.

104
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:21,610
i is the quarter turn.

105
00:03:22,080 --> 00:03:23,900
One goes to i, straight up.

106
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,660
i goes to negative one.

107
00:03:25,910 --> 00:03:27,580
Negative one goes down to

108
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:29,900
negative i, and then back to one.

109
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:32,500
i times i is negative one.

110
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:35,120
Not as a rule to memorize, but because

111
00:03:35,240 --> 00:03:36,950
two quarter turns make a half turn.

112
00:03:37,690 --> 00:03:39,300
And multiplying by i

113
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:40,500
turns the whole plane.

114
00:03:40,900 --> 00:03:43,150
Every arrow, rotated ninety degrees.

115
00:03:45,060 --> 00:03:47,110
Now we can read e to the i t.

116
00:03:48,160 --> 00:03:49,700
Remember the rule for e to the t.

117
00:03:50,010 --> 00:03:51,560
Velocity equals position.

118
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:53,780
For e to the i t, the

119
00:03:53,820 --> 00:03:55,250
rule picks up a single i.

120
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:58,553
Velocity equals i times position.

121
00:03:58,553 --> 00:03:59,620
And we know what i does.

122
00:03:59,890 --> 00:04:02,340
It turns an arrow by a quarter turn.

123
00:04:02,340 --> 00:04:04,260
So the velocity is always the

124
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,740
position, turned ninety degrees.

125
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:07,350
Let us watch.

126
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:09,933
Start at one, on the real line.

127
00:04:09,933 --> 00:04:11,340
The position arrow points right.

128
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:13,550
So the velocity points straight up.

129
00:04:14,380 --> 00:04:15,590
The point moves up.

130
00:04:15,850 --> 00:04:17,820
As it moves, its position arrow

131
00:04:17,940 --> 00:04:19,910
tilts, so the velocity tilts too.

132
00:04:20,390 --> 00:04:21,790
Always at a right angle.

133
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:24,230
Always pushing sideways, never outward.

134
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,960
A push that is always sideways

135
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:28,440
can never bring you closer,

136
00:04:28,480 --> 00:04:29,780
or carry you farther away.

137
00:04:30,060 --> 00:04:32,000
So the point stays exactly

138
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:33,160
one unit from the center.

139
00:04:33,550 --> 00:04:34,730
It traces a circle.

140
00:04:35,670 --> 00:04:37,380
And how fast does it go?

141
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:38,740
The velocity has the same

142
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:39,720
length as the position.

143
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:40,430
One.

144
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,980
So the point walks around the circle at

145
00:04:43,060 --> 00:04:45,140
one unit of distance, per unit of time.

146
00:04:46,100 --> 00:04:48,180
Let the whole plane follow the same rule.

147
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:49,880
Ordinary growth sends

148
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:51,410
every point flying outward.

149
00:04:51,700 --> 00:04:53,160
Turn the growth part of the

150
00:04:53,200 --> 00:04:54,440
way, and the points spiral.

151
00:04:54,730 --> 00:04:57,080
Turn it all the way, to i, and

152
00:04:57,160 --> 00:04:58,790
every point circles forever.

153
00:04:59,620 --> 00:05:02,620
So e to the i t has a simple meaning.

154
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:04,890
Walk along the unit circle, a distance t.

155
00:05:05,810 --> 00:05:07,330
Now, pause and predict.

156
00:05:07,730 --> 00:05:08,590
We start at one.

157
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:10,320
How far do we have to walk

158
00:05:10,360 --> 00:05:11,260
to reach negative one?

159
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:16,380
Halfway around a circle of radius one.

160
00:05:16,770 --> 00:05:18,580
The full way around is two pi.

161
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,980
So halfway, is pi.

162
00:05:20,980 --> 00:05:22,370
After walking a distance pi,

163
00:05:22,590 --> 00:05:24,290
the point lands on negative one.

164
00:05:24,710 --> 00:05:27,070
e to the i pi equals negative one.

165
00:05:27,370 --> 00:05:28,080
A half turn.

166
00:05:28,290 --> 00:05:29,460
Which is exactly what

167
00:05:29,540 --> 00:05:30,960
we said negative one is.

168
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:32,850
That is the picture.

169
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:34,500
But a picture can fool you.

170
00:05:34,790 --> 00:05:36,370
So let us check it, twice,

171
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:38,280
using nothing but arithmetic.

172
00:05:39,700 --> 00:05:40,820
Go back to the bank.

173
00:05:41,380 --> 00:05:42,850
e came from compounding.

174
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:45,790
One plus one over n, raised to the n.

175
00:05:46,110 --> 00:05:48,260
So e to the i pi should

176
00:05:48,340 --> 00:05:49,910
come from compounding i pi.

177
00:05:50,380 --> 00:05:53,240
One plus i pi over n, raised to the n.

178
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:55,230
Start crude.

179
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:56,640
Let n be one.

180
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:58,290
One plus i pi.

181
00:05:58,530 --> 00:06:00,930
That is a point far up and to the right.

182
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:02,700
Nowhere near negative one.

183
00:06:03,770 --> 00:06:04,720
Let n be two.

184
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:07,420
Multiplying by one plus i pi over

185
00:06:07,500 --> 00:06:09,060
two turns the plane a little,

186
00:06:09,270 --> 00:06:10,380
and stretches it a little.

187
00:06:10,750 --> 00:06:12,890
Do that twice, and we land up here.

188
00:06:14,010 --> 00:06:14,870
Four steps.

189
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:17,040
Each one a smaller turn,

190
00:06:17,080 --> 00:06:18,160
and a smaller stretch.

191
00:06:18,630 --> 00:06:20,060
The path begins to bend.

192
00:06:21,210 --> 00:06:21,940
Eight steps.

193
00:06:22,450 --> 00:06:23,190
Sixteen.

194
00:06:23,720 --> 00:06:24,360
A hundred.

195
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:26,850
The stretches shrink toward nothing.

196
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,740
The turns add up closer

197
00:06:28,820 --> 00:06:30,660
and closer to a half turn.

198
00:06:30,700 --> 00:06:32,820
And the path hugs the unit circle,

199
00:06:32,900 --> 00:06:34,440
sliding into its final spot.

200
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:36,280
Negative one.

201
00:06:37,390 --> 00:06:39,490
Compounding a rate of growth gives e.

202
00:06:39,970 --> 00:06:41,500
Compounding a rate of turning

203
00:06:41,553 --> 00:06:42,820
gives a walk around the circle.

204
00:06:44,810 --> 00:06:45,720
There is a second way

205
00:06:45,800 --> 00:06:47,070
to compute e to the x.

206
00:06:47,400 --> 00:06:48,680
An infinite sum.

207
00:06:49,020 --> 00:06:52,040
One, plus x, plus x squared over two,

208
00:06:52,160 --> 00:06:54,920
plus x cubed over six, and so on.

209
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:57,720
Each term is x to the n, over n factorial.

210
00:06:58,650 --> 00:07:01,020
Plug in i pi, and treat each term

211
00:07:01,100 --> 00:07:02,850
as an arrow, laid tip to tail.

212
00:07:03,860 --> 00:07:05,140
The first term is one.

213
00:07:05,350 --> 00:07:06,270
A step to the right.

214
00:07:07,360 --> 00:07:08,810
The second is i pi.

215
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:11,380
The i turns it a quarter turn, so

216
00:07:11,460 --> 00:07:13,450
we step straight up, a distance pi.

217
00:07:14,570 --> 00:07:16,200
The third has i squared,

218
00:07:16,320 --> 00:07:17,507
which turns twice.

219
00:07:17,533 --> 00:07:18,450
So it points left.

220
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:19,860
Pi squared over two.

221
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:21,320
About four point nine.

222
00:07:22,250 --> 00:07:24,670
The next turns again, and points down.

223
00:07:24,990 --> 00:07:25,510
Then right.

224
00:07:25,830 --> 00:07:26,370
Then up.

225
00:07:26,890 --> 00:07:28,910
Each new step turns one more quarter.

226
00:07:29,890 --> 00:07:31,627
At first, the steps grow,

227
00:07:31,653 --> 00:07:33,170
and the path swings far away.

228
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:34,960
But the factorials grow

229
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,680
faster than any power of pi.

230
00:07:36,970 --> 00:07:38,960
Soon the steps shrink, and the

231
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,160
path spirals inward, closer

232
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:42,520
and closer to one point.

233
00:07:43,530 --> 00:07:44,800
Negative one, again.

234
00:07:46,010 --> 00:07:48,427
And look at the horizontal steps.

235
00:07:48,467 --> 00:07:50,270
Together, they add up to the cosine of pi.

236
00:07:50,770 --> 00:07:51,880
The vertical steps add

237
00:07:51,960 --> 00:07:52,960
up to the sine of pi.

238
00:07:53,220 --> 00:07:54,170
Which is zero.

239
00:07:56,010 --> 00:07:57,967
Pi was never special.

240
00:07:58,073 --> 00:07:59,540
Walk any distance theta, and you

241
00:07:59,660 --> 00:08:01,380
land somewhere on the circle.

242
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:02,780
How far right are you?

243
00:08:03,070 --> 00:08:04,490
That is the cosine of theta.

244
00:08:04,890 --> 00:08:05,610
How far up?

245
00:08:05,950 --> 00:08:06,750
The sine of theta.

246
00:08:07,050 --> 00:08:09,800
So e to the i theta equals cosine

247
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:12,640
theta, plus i times sine theta.

248
00:08:12,640 --> 00:08:13,850
This is Euler's formula.

249
00:08:14,810 --> 00:08:16,860
Now let time run, and spread the

250
00:08:16,980 --> 00:08:18,490
walk out along a third direction.

251
00:08:18,750 --> 00:08:21,490
The point traces a spiral, a helix.

252
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,020
Look from the side, and

253
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,020
you see a sine wave.

254
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:26,160
Look from below, a cosine wave.

255
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:28,460
Look head on, and it collapses

256
00:08:28,540 --> 00:08:29,390
back into the circle.

257
00:08:30,290 --> 00:08:32,400
This is why circles hide inside so

258
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:33,820
much of physics and engineering.

259
00:08:34,160 --> 00:08:37,387
Springs, alternating current, sound.

260
00:08:37,493 --> 00:08:38,880
Wherever something oscillates, there

261
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:40,930
is often a turning arrow underneath.

262
00:08:41,720 --> 00:08:43,570
Now try a few special values.

263
00:08:44,080 --> 00:08:46,580
Theta equals pi over two, a quarter

264
00:08:46,620 --> 00:08:48,690
of the way around, and you land on i.

265
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,330
Theta equals pi, halfway,

266
00:08:51,590 --> 00:08:53,040
and you land on negative one.

267
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,940
Theta equals two pi, all the way

268
00:08:55,980 --> 00:08:57,760
around, and you are back at one.

269
00:08:58,800 --> 00:09:00,520
And multiplying by e to the i

270
00:09:00,680 --> 00:09:02,650
theta does not just move one point.

271
00:09:02,860 --> 00:09:05,350
It turns the entire plane by theta.

272
00:09:05,680 --> 00:09:07,480
e to the i pi turns

273
00:09:07,560 --> 00:09:09,010
everything by half a turn.

274
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:11,500
Move the one across, and

275
00:09:11,540 --> 00:09:12,780
you get the famous form.

276
00:09:13,230 --> 00:09:16,120
e to the i pi, plus one, equals zero.

277
00:09:18,310 --> 00:09:20,520
So let us read the equation one last time.

278
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:24,560
e is growth whose rate equals its size.

279
00:09:25,050 --> 00:09:26,400
i is a quarter turn.

280
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:27,900
Put them together, and

281
00:09:27,980 --> 00:09:29,570
the growth turns sideways.

282
00:09:29,780 --> 00:09:31,660
Instead of running away, the point

283
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:34,020
walks around a circle, at speed one.

284
00:09:35,020 --> 00:09:36,510
Pi is the distance.

285
00:09:36,850 --> 00:09:39,200
Walk pi, and you have gone halfway around.

286
00:09:39,520 --> 00:09:41,360
And a half turn is exactly

287
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,590
what negative one means.

288
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,460
The bank, the infinite sum,

289
00:09:45,540 --> 00:09:47,010
and the picture all agree.

290
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:50,350
e to the i pi equals negative one.

291
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:52,340
Not a coincidence of symbols.

292
00:09:52,670 --> 00:09:53,500
A half turn.

293
00:09:54,610 --> 00:09:55,980
If you want to see what happens when

294
00:09:56,100 --> 00:09:57,500
many of these turning arrows are added

295
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,910
together, that is the Fourier series,

296
00:10:00,170 --> 00:10:02,220
and that is where we are going next.
